The incident has a single fault: the search→rate connection, where about 1.5 s is added before rate starts handling the request. Its effect reaches the user through `frontend` `/hotels`. Profile and reservation are at normal levels.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "search",
      "fault_kind": "network_delay",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, attr_span_kind, span_name, count(*) n, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.5)/1e6,2) p50_ms, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.95)/1e6,2) p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE span_name IN ('rate.Rate/GetRates','search.Search/Nearby') GROUP BY ALL ORDER BY 1,2",
          "claim": "search's client span to rate takes p50 ~1538ms, while rate's server span for the same calls takes ~0.6ms."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, attr_span_kind, span_name, count(*) n, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.5)/1e6,2) p50_ms FROM normal_traces WHERE span_name IN ('rate.Rate/GetRates','search.Search/Nearby') GROUP BY ALL ORDER BY 1,2",
          "claim": "In the normal period search's client span to rate was ~0.9ms p50, so the ~1.5s gap is new."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, floor((epoch(time) - (SELECT min(epoch(time)) FROM abnormal_traces))/120) AS bucket2m, count(*) n, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.5)/1e6,2) p50_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE (service_name='search' AND span_name LIKE 'rate.%') GROUP BY ALL ORDER BY 1,2,3",
          "claim": "The search→rate delay is flat at ~1530-1550ms p50 across every two-minute bucket of the incident."
        },
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT metric, service_name, round(avg(value),4) avg_v FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE service_name IN ('search','rate') AND metric LIKE '%cpu.usage' GROUP BY ALL ORDER BY 2,1",
          "claim": "search and rate container CPU is low during the incident, so this is not CPU saturation of either end."
        },
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT metric, service_name, attr_k8s_pod_name pod, round(min(value),2) mn, round(max(value),2) mx FROM normal_metrics WHERE metric='k8s.container.restarts' AND attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'rate%' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "rate's restart count is the same (13) in both periods, so rate did not restart during the incident."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "search",
      "to": "frontend",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.5)/1e6,2) p50_ms, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.95)/1e6,2) p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE span_name IN ('HTTP /hotels','search.Search/Nearby') GROUP BY ALL ORDER BY 1,3",
          "claim": "frontend's HTTP /hotels server span (~1545ms p50) matches its search.Search/Nearby client span, which matches search's own server span."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

